{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הבא", :translit "havi", :gloss "bring"} {:he "הבא את האנשים הביתה", :translit "havi et ha-anashim ha-baytah", :gloss "bring the men home"} {:he "הבא העיר", :translit "havi ha-ir", :gloss "come to the city"} {:he "הבא ידך", :translit "havi yadekha", :gloss "bring your hand"} {:he "כעיר שחוברה לה יחדו", :translit "ke-ir she-chubrah lah yachdav", :gloss "like a city that is joined together"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הבא" "הבא את האנשים הביתה" "הבא העיר"]}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim presents a typological reading of the three occurrences of the word הבא. Each instance is linked to a key figure in the drama of exile and redemption: Jonathan (or Joseph) whose actions brought the family down to Egypt (Genesis 43:16), Moses who brought them out, and a future figure associated with the ingathering to Jerusalem. Jerusalem is identified as the city described in Psalms 122:3.", :sources ["Genesis 43:16" "Psalms 122:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בחיקך", :translit "be-cheikcha", :gloss "in your bosom"} {:he "ואתנה וגו' נשי אדוניך בחיקך", :translit "ve-etnah vi-gomer n'shei adoneikha be-cheikcha", :gloss "and I will give etc. your master's wives into your bosom"} {:he "ושכבה בחיקך", :translit "u-shchavah be-cheikcha", :gloss "and lie in your bosom"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["בחיקך" "נשי אדוניך בחיקך" "ושכבה בחיקך"]} {:kind :other, :note "Comparison: just as Moses was stricken with tzara'at (Exodus 4:6), so Ruth was stricken with tzara'at for six months"}], :frame {:text "The word בחיקך occurs three times in Scripture. The Ba'al HaTurim draws a connection between Moses being stricken with tzara'at and a tradition that Ruth was afflicted with tzara'at for six months. The name Ruth appears in the rendering, and the verse citations point to II Samuel 12:8 and 12:11; the specific midrashic source for the six-month affliction of Ruth is not named.", :sources ["II Samuel 1